1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:04,723
Get ready for a big one!

2
00:00:04,723 --> 00:00:17,210
We start in the highest city in America, climb over the Continental Divide at twelve thousand ninety-five feet, explore a real gold rush ghost town, and finish in Aspen!

3
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:24,823
This is Independence Pass: 57 miles from Leadville to Aspen, right over the Continental Divide.

4
00:00:24,823 --> 00:00:28,470
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

5
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:30,574
Here's the plan!

6
00:00:30,574 --> 00:00:38,290
We leave Leadville, stop at Twin Lakes, climb Independence Pass, explore a ghost town, and roll into Aspen!

7
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:47,525
We're starting in Leadville, the highest incorporated city in America, at ten thousand one hundred fifty-two feet!

8
00:00:47,525 --> 00:00:52,685
Back in the silver boom, this was one of the richest towns in the West.

9
00:00:52,685 --> 00:00:53,920
Okay, let's roll!

10
00:00:54,870 --> 00:00:57,898
We head south down the Arkansas River valley.

11
00:00:57,898 --> 00:00:59,716
Look out your right window!

12
00:00:59,716 --> 00:01:06,580
That giant is Mount Elbert, the tallest peak in Colorado, at over fourteen thousand four hundred feet!

13
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:09,009
Welcome to Twin Lakes!

14
00:01:09,009 --> 00:01:14,186
Two sparkling glacial lakes, with Colorado's tallest peaks right behind them.

15
00:01:14,186 --> 00:01:18,690
This little village was a stop on the old wagon road over the pass.

16
00:01:19,640 --> 00:01:21,299
Now the climb begins!

17
00:01:21,299 --> 00:01:27,223
We follow Lake Creek up the valley, then switchback our way above treeline.

18
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:29,040
Hold on, it gets steep!

19
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:30,852
We made it!

20
00:01:30,852 --> 00:01:37,509
Independence Pass, twelve thousand ninety-five feet, right on the Continental Divide!

21
00:01:37,509 --> 00:01:41,190
Walk the short paved trail out to the overlook.

22
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:43,070
The views go on forever!

23
00:01:44,020 --> 00:01:45,827
Down the west side we go!

24
00:01:45,827 --> 00:01:52,550
That little stream is the Roaring Fork River, and it's about to lead us all the way to Aspen!

25
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:57,312
This is Independence, a gold rush town from 1879!

26
00:01:57,312 --> 00:02:03,691
Miners struck gold here around the Fourth of July, and that's how it got its name.

27
00:02:03,691 --> 00:02:05,869
Walk through the old cabins.

28
00:02:05,869 --> 00:02:06,880
It's so cool!

29
00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:13,933
Now it's down the Roaring Fork Valley, with a couple of tight one-lane squeezes, so take it slow!

30
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:19,470
Then stop at the Grottos, with waterfalls and ice caves just a short walk from the road!

31
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:21,514
Welcome to Aspen!

32
00:02:21,514 --> 00:02:28,076
It started as a silver mining camp, and today it's one of the most famous mountain towns in the world.

33
00:02:28,076 --> 00:02:31,679
If you have time, the Maroon Bells are just up the road.

34
00:02:31,679 --> 00:02:33,030
What a way to finish!

35
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:35,658
And that's the drive!

36
00:02:35,658 --> 00:02:42,210
57 miles from Leadville to Aspen, topping out at 12,095 feet on Independence Pass.

37
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:46,320
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

38
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:48,090
Pause and grab a screenshot!

39
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:53,410
Thanks for riding along!

40
00:02:53,410 --> 00:02:58,370
Hit subscribe, and next time we're driving the Peak to Peak Highway!
